 **************************************************************** 4125 1451
 Resolved and unresolved resonance parameters replaced by those   4125 1451
 in JENDL-4.0, and the resolved resonance boundary energy         4125 1451
 changed from 7.35keV to 7keV. The comment section in JENDL-4.0   4125 1451
 about the resonance evaluation is copied below.                  4125 1451
                                            T. Kawano, Oct. 2016  4125 1451
                                                                  4125 1451
MF=2          Resonance parameters                                4125 1451
  MT=151 Resolved and unresolved resonance parameters             4125 1451
    Resolved resonances: 1.0e-5 eV - 7 keV                        4125 1451
      Parameters in JENDL-3.1 were taken from JENDL-2 by modifying4125 1451
      J values. The JENDL-2 parameters were evaluated on the basis4125 1451
      of following measurements:                                  4125 1451
       transmission  by Garg et al./12/, Poittevin et al./13/     4125 1451
                     and Iliescu et al./14/                       4125 1451
       scattering    by Iliescu et al./14/                        4125 1451
       capture       by Macklin /15/, Lopez et al./16/ and        4125 1451
                     Iliescu et al. /14/                          4125 1451
      J values determined by Haste et al. /17/  were adopted.     4125 1451
      average radiative width was assumed to be 0.172 eV (0.212 eV4125 1451
      for doublet), and Scattering radius to be 7.10 fm.  The J   4125 1451
      values of resonances without known j values were randomly   4125 1451
      assigned.                                                   4125 1451
                                                                  4125 1451
      For JENDL-3.2, re-assignment of J and modification of       4125 1451
      neutron and radiative widths were made to reproduce the     4125 1451
      measured capture area data/15/.                             4125 1451
                                                                  4125 1451
      In JENDL-4.0, we took account of the data for eight         4125 1451
      resonances obtained by Drindak et al./18/  The J values     4125 1451
      for 364.93-eV s-wave, 362.71-eV p-wave and 392,53-eV p-wave 4125 1451
      resonances were taken from ENDF/B-VI.8.                     4125 1451
                                                                  4125 1451
      After JENDL-3.3 evaluation, new measurements 93Nb resonance 4125 1451
      parameters have been made by Drindak et al./18/ and by      4125 1451
      Wang et al./19/.                                            4125 1451
      Resonance parameters of JENDL-3.3 are replaced by           4125 1451
      those of Drindak et al./18/ in the resonance energy region  4125 1451
      below 500eV, in detail, an s-wave resonance at Er=194.25 eV;4125 1451
      J=4 was added and a p-wave resonance at Er=184.3 eV was     4125 1451
      eliminated.                                                 4125 1451
      Resonance parameters of a negative resonance were determined4125 1451
      to reproduce thermal cross sections and resonance integral  4125 1451
      given by Mughabghab/20/.                                    4125 1451
                                                                  4125 1451
  Unresolved resonances: 7 keV - 600 keV                          4125 1451
     Determined with the asrep code/21/ so as to reproduce        4125 1451
     the evaluated sig-c and sig-t up to 600 keV.                 4125 1451
                                                                  4125 1451
     Typical parameters at 70 keV:                                4125 1451
       s0= 0.4e-4, s1=6.68e-4, d-obs=96.0 ev, r=6.477 fm,         4125 1451
       radiative width= 0.172 eV                                  4125 1451
                                                                  4125 1451
    The parameters should be used only for self-shielding         4125 1451
    calculation.                                                  4125 1451
                                                                  4125 1451
